{"rubric_version":"opencode-browser-856867996e73f7dcc5e39827bf2af7555bd63d40-judge-prompt.md","attempt":1,"prompt":[{"role":"system","content":"# WebVoyager Benchmark Evaluation\n\nYou are an evaluator for a web browsing agent benchmark. You will receive:\n\n1. **WebVoyager_data.json** — the task definitions (task_id, confirmed_task, website)\n2. **results.ndjson** — the agent's execution results (one JSON per line)\n\n## Your Job\n\nFor each result in results.ndjson, judge whether the agent successfully completed the task.\n\n## Evaluation Rules\n\n**PASS** if:\n- The agent's `final_answer` contains the specific information requested by the task\n- The information is factually plausible (e.g., a recipe with \"4.5 stars\" when task asks for \"at least 4.5 stars\")\n- Minor formatting differences, extra information, or verbose answers are acceptable\n- Partial completion counts as PASS only if the core requirement is met\n\n**FAIL** if:\n- `status` is \"error\" or \"timeout\" AND `final_answer` is empty or does not answer the task\n- The answer is wrong, irrelevant, or hallucinatory\n- The answer is generic (e.g., \"I found a recipe\" without providing the actual recipe details)\n- The agent failed to find the requested information and said so\n- Key requirements are missing (e.g., task asks for \"rating above 4.5\" but agent's answer shows a 3-star recipe)\n\n**NOTE**: If `status` is \"error\" but `final_answer` still contains a valid answer to the task, judge it as PASS.\n\n## Output Format\n\nReturn a JSON array, one object per task:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"task_id\": \"Allrecipes--0\",\n    \"pass\": true,\n    \"reason\": \"Agent found a vegetarian lasagna recipe with 4.6 stars and 150+ reviews, matching all criteria.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"task_id\": \"Allrecipes--1\",\n    \"pass\": false,\n    \"reason\": \"Agent returned a lasagna recipe but it does not use zucchini as required.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nRequirements for each entry:\n- `task_id`: must match exactly\n- `pass`: boolean\n- `reason`: one sentence explaining why pass or fail, referencing the specific task requirement\n\n## Important\n\n- Compare `final_answer` against `confirmed_task` from WebVoyager_data.json for each matching `task_id`\n- Do NOT skip any result — every entry in results.ndjson must have a judgment\n- Be strict on whether the core task requirement is met, but lenient on presentation\n- If the task asks for multiple things (e.g., \"find a recipe AND list ingredients\"), all parts must be present to PASS\n\nEvaluate all results now.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"WebVoyager_data.json\n[{\"task_id\":\"Huggingface--21\",\"confirmed_task\":\"Look up the tour about how to use the 'pipeline' feature in the Hugging Face Transformers library for sentiment analysis, and identify the default model it uses.\",\"website\":\"https://huggingface.co/\"}]\n\nresults.ndjson\n{\"task_id\":\"Huggingface--21\",\"website\":\"https://huggingface.co/\",\"task\":\"Look up the tour about how to use the 'pipeline' feature in the Hugging Face Transformers library for sentiment analysis, and identify the default model it uses.\",\"session_id\":\"eval-Huggingface--21-ca502ae5a628\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"duration_ms\":405308,\"steps\":45,\"tokens\":{\"input\":189636,\"output\":14709,\"cache_read\":537461,\"cache_write\":0,\"reasoning\":9292},\"cost\":0.10678926000000001,\"final_answer\":\"Based on my research, I have found the answer to the task. Let me provide a comprehensive response.\\n\\n## Summary of Findings\\n\\n**The Tour**: The Quicktour page (https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/quicktour) in the Hugging Face Transformers documentation includes a section specifically about the `pipeline()` feature. It demonstrates sentiment analysis with this code:\\n\\n```python\\n>>> from transformers import pipeline\\n>>> classifier = pipeline(\\\"sentiment-analysis\\\")\\n```\\n\\nThe tour states: *\\\"The pipeline() downloads and caches a default pretrained model and tokenizer for sentiment analysis.\\\"*\\n\\n**Default Model for Sentiment Analysis**: The default pretrained model that `pipeline(\\\"sentiment-analysis\\\")` downloads and uses is **`distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english`**.\\n\\nThis is confirmed by:\\n1. The API documentation example for `TextClassificationPipeline`, which explicitly shows:\\n   ```python\\n   >>> classifier = pipeline(model=\\\"distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english\\\")\\n   >>> classifier(\\\"This movie is disgustingly good !\\\")\\n   [{'label': 'POSITIVE', 'score': 1.0}]\\n   ```\\n2. This model is a fine-tuned version of DistilBERT on the SST-2 (Stanford Sentiment Treebank) dataset, optimized for binary sentiment classification (POSITIVE/NEGATIVE).\\n\\n## Note on Research Process\\nWhile the Quicktour narrative says \\\"a default pretrained model\\\" without explicitly naming it, the well-known default configured in the Transformers library's `SUPPORTED_TASKS` dictionary for the `sentiment-analysis` (alias for `text-classification`) task is `distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english`. The API reference documentation explicitly uses this model in its example, confirming it as the canonical default.\",\"tool_trace\":[{\"tool\":\"browser_goto\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0df13c1d872a1ab754bed\",\"time_ms\":5,\"output_preview\":\"Error: browser_goto failed: Browser not started. Call browser_start first to enter browser mode.\\nSafe retry: verify browser_start succeeded, refresh the DOM snapshot, and retry once with current element/tab IDs.\\nStop condition: stop retrying if Chromium is unavailable, approval is denied, or the sam\",\"status\":\"error\"},{\"tool\":\"browser_start\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main_classes/pipelines\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0df13c5cd7442a27cf493\",\"time_ms\":30665,\"output_preview\":\"# Browser Mode\\n\\nThe DSH browser plugin controls